In <33A5857D.23B4C2F9@uccs.jpl.nasa.gov> Frank Maritato <frank@uccs.jpl.nasa.gov> writes:

>    My keyboard generates a "^?" when I hit the backspace key.

This is because your keyboard has no backspace key.  That is the delete
key.

>Now, on the
>terminal I can type "stty erase ^?" to generate the erase action, but in
>the vi editor
>I still get a "^?". Is there any way I can map "^?" to "^H" in vi?

If you do it properly at the shell level, i.e. 

    stty erase ^\?
or
    stty erase '^?'

vi will "understand" it and no special setting is required.

If you're in an X environment (workstation or X terminal), you can
remap the delete key to be the backspace key.  Use xmodmap or the user
friendly interface, dxkeycaps.

