Marc Tillinghast (tilly@storm.com) wrote:

: I've got a problem with LMF on an Alpha onto which I just installed Digital
: Unix
: version 4.0B.  I can't get the OSF-BASE package correctly configured.  I'm
: sure
: that I'm typing all the license information correctly, but when I attempt
: to register
: the package, the product never leaves the "enabled" state.  

: Typing 'lmf list' returns the following:

: # lmf list

: Product                          Status                  Users: Total      
: Active

: OSF-BASE                      enabled                   
: MMS-RT                        active                          unlimited
: NET-APP-SUP-150               active                          unlimited
: OPEN3D                        active                          unlimited
: OSF-DEV                       active                          unlimited
: OSF-USR                       active                        4      0    

: If I type 'lmf reset' I get the following response:

: # lmf reset
: Not enough units to load OSF-BASE DEC

: What are these 'units'?  Is there a kernal parm I need to modify?
: Any help would be appreciated.

Marc,

Each OSF-BASE PAK has X number of units which you can see by
issuing this command:

# lmf list full for OSF-BASE

           Product Name: OSF-BASE
               Producer: DEC
                 Issuer: DEC
   Authorization Number: ALS-NQ-1996FEB23-1089
        Number of units: 2700
                Version:
   Product Release Date:
   Key Termination Date:
Availability Table Code: A
    Activity Table Code:
            Key Options: MOD_UNITS, ALPHA
          Product Token:
            Hardware-Id:
         License status: active, multiple
      Cancellation Date:
        Revision Number: 0
                Comment:

The units are cumulitive and you need a certain amount depending
on the configuration (number of CPU's, etc) of the system. For
example, on an 8400 with 8 CPU's, I have four OSF-BASE license
PAKS, one with 2700 units and three additional with 200 units
each. You "should" have the add'l required PAK's, but if you
don't, you should contact DEC or who ever sold you the system
to obtain the remaining PAK(s).

Hope this helps a bit.
Matt
