> I have recently updated my graphics board from a 4d20 to a 4d60 on my
> DEC Alpha 500/400. 
> [Overlay problem deleted]

Congratulations on your very substantial upgrade.  The 60T does indeed
have a double buffered overlay but not Z buffered.  If your program
is expecting a Z buffer, it will be sorely disappointed.  Use xglinfo to
identify the correct overlay visual.  If all else fails, you could make this
the default visual and try your program again.  And make certain there's
nothing screwy with your swap buffers call.


