John,

The file you are looking for is called /etc/securettys.  This file
controls whether there are root logins from any where other than the
console.

By default the /etc/securettys file is set  up with:

/dev/console
local:0
:0
this is to enable the console for root login.

If you want to login as root via telnet put the entry "ptys" in the
file.

Also if you are using X-windows or a X-windows emulator and you want to
login as root you must add the entry "<hostname:0> to the file.
For instance if the hostname for your X-windows workstation is "wks100"
you would enter this in the file:

wks100:0

I hope this helps.

-Steve


