John D. Brown (jdbrown@wavenet.com) wrote:
: What file controls root login? I'm using a x-win32 emulator under win95. I
: get this message only when logging in as root:
: "root login refused on this terminal."
: Thanks

John,

Direct root logins are allowed/disallowed using the /etc/securettys
file. This file list the valid places that root may login from. By
default this file allows direct root login from:

/dev/console
local:0
:0

To allow root logins from across the network, simply append the
following string to the end of /etc/securettys:

ptys

