The principle is that the 'odd' lettered (a c e g ...) ones are mainly
about hardware, that is, required for new workstations / servers /
devices.  There is no normally need to install those unless you
explicitly know that for example your new workstation needs them.
Moreover, your new workstation should have that level factory
installed anyway.  For example when 4.0 came out it did not support
all the latest hardware.  For those the 4.0a was produced.

The 'even' lettered one (b d f ...) are then more software-oriented.
They fix software bugs, update documentation, things like that.

For patches: go to http://www.service.digital.com/ and right there in
the first page are the instructions on how to subscribe for the patch
announcement mailing lists.

