Sirio Candini wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> running C and TCL/TK programs in our systems, sometimes we get
> the next message:
> 
> DECthreads bugcheck (version V3.13-435), terminating execution.
> vpUpcallThreadUnblocked: (os/kern) invalid argument (4)
> nxm_resched(11,0)
> 
> Our systems are Digital Alpha with DEC UNIX 4.0B.
> 
> Have you any suggest?

This is a sporadic problem where a kernel function returns an "error
status" that's actually benign in the current context. The DECthreads
library incorrectly complains about the unexpected situation.

Install the June patch kit to fix this problem.

ftp://ftp.service.digital.com/public/Digital_UNIX/v4.0b/
	duv40bas00004-19970609.tar	Kit
	duv40bas00004-19970609.README	Documentation

In particular, the patch ID you want is OSF410-400195.

