On 21 Jun 1997 19:04:34 GMT, "John D. Brown" <jdbrown@wavenet.com>
wrote:

>What file controls root login? I'm using a x-win32 emulator under win95. I
>get this message only when logging in as root:
>"root login refused on this terminal."
>Thanks
Assuming, that you do not have "Enhanced Security" installed on your
system, the file /etc/securettys controls root logins.
Use "man securettys" to get more info.

But note, that you can only allow _ALL_ network-pseudo-terminals or
NONE. If set, you can log in as root from everywhere, which may not be
secure.
