Christian Rossi (chris@genesis.cib.unibo.it) wrote:
> Hi, 

> I have Digital Unix 4.0B and when I turn on my machine
> it doesn't make the automatically reboot.
> It will be a software problem (I think) ,
> because with old OS version it were ok.
> Someone can help me?
> Thanks af all.

Christian,

I can only assume you mean that the system does not
automatically boot when you power it on... correct?
If so, you are probably placed at the triple-chevron
prompt (P01>>>).

There are several console variables you need to check
and possibly set: auto_action, boot_dev, and boot_osflags

Type "show auto_action" to see the value of auto_action.
It should say BOOT. If it does not, type "set auto_action BOOT"

Also, check boot_dev and boot_osflags in a similar manner.

boot_dev should be assigned to your primary boot disk as
shown by the "show devices" command.

boot_osflags should be set to the letter "a" (which causes
it to boot automatically to multi-user.)

Hope this helps.
Matt
