In article <33986C7D.41C67EA6@sunrem.com>, Brandon Gillespie <brandon@sunrem.com> writes:

>Is it possible to do multiple backups with vdump on a single tape?

Yes.

You can use the 'f' option and specify the no-rewind tape device
or read the manual page and use the -N option, which will tell
vdump to use the norewind tape device for you.  Example:

	vdump 0uf /dev/nrmt0h /first-file-system
	vdump 0uf /dev/nrmt0h /second-file-system
	...

From the manual page, I assume these are the same as:

	vdump 0uN /first-file-system
	vdump 0uN /second-file-system
>
>-Brandon
