Been there, done that...

nslookup uses its own routines for resolving names, not the actual
BIND resolver library.  Your /etc/svc.conf is not configured
correctly.  Check out its man page and that of svcsetup.  It's a good
idea to leave 'local' as the first option, e.g. hosts=local,bind. The
default does not include bind at all.  The bindsetup script should take
care of all of this too.

-Robert



