Graham Jones <graham@xliteyear.demon.co.uk> wrote:
}I am having trouble printing from an Alpha 8200 running DU4.0A to a third
}party print server.
}We have just installed a new printer server, which I believe is called barr
}spool  / barr print 370
}When we print single documents to server they get spooled off just fine.
}However, if more than one print job is in the
}queue all but the first job gets 'lost'.
}The manufacturers think that DU is sending only 1 lpd header with the print
}jobs, and this is confusing the print server.
}Does anyone know of similar problems of this nature. Or if there is a way
}to force lpd to send a header with each job.

    The LPD protocol allows for multiple jobs to be sent
    in the same connection -- sounds like the 'barr spool'
    thingy is out-of-spec -- quoting from RFC1179:

        6. Receive job subcommands
 
           These commands are processed when the line printer daemon has
           been given the receive job command.  The daemon will continue
           to process commands until the connection is closed.

John
