Rob Millner <rmillner@pongo.cv.nrao.edu> wrote:
>How do I get the monster libc (Patch 80.00, OSF410-400189, SSRT0425U,
>SSRT0296U) patch to install on my system if I don't have (don't need,
>hence don't have) OSFUUCP410 installed?  It needs to patch files in the
>UUCP distribution but those files are not themselves depended upon for
>any other parts of the patch.  Thanks.

I have opened up a trouble call on this with DEC.  The person I spoke to
had me try to "trick" dupatch into believing UUCP was installed by
creating the file /usr/.smdb./OSFUUCP410.lk but unfortunately this 
didn't work because dupatch checked for the existence of the actual files
within the UUCP subset which it wants to patch.

The person I worked with on this agreed with me that it is ridiculous that
I have to install a subset that I don't want or need on my system, in order to
be able to install a patch I do want and need.  He is going to put in a request
to engineering that they fix this behavior of dupatch.  In the interim, it
appears the only solution is to install UUCP.  Obviously you don't have to
configure or use it if you don't want.  And you can even uninstall it after
applying the patch.  This is a hassle IMO but I don't see an alternative so
that is the path I have chosen to take.
