Anthony McGarr wrote:
> 
> Version 4.0b.C2 enabled .. How do you unlock a user account from the
> command line.
> Due to a bug in the cde we cannot use dxaccounts.
> 
It's pretty simple:

dxaccounts puts a 'Nologin' string in front of the encrypted password.
Therefore you can use vi/sed or whatever you like to remove these
strings. Here is an example:

user:NologindnEKsA/UL7ho.:7119:9115:Mr. User:/home/user:/bin/tcsh

sed -e 's/user:Nologin/user:/' passwd > passwd.unlocked 

should do the job in this case.

Best wishes,

Torsten Hehl.



