Anthony McGarr (delphig@dsuper.net) wrote:
> Version 4.0b.C2 enabled .. How do you unlock a user account from the
> command line.
> Due to a bug in the cde we cannot use dxaccounts.

Anthony,

As root, run the following:

/usr/tcb/bin/edauth userid (of course substituting the user account name)

This should pop you into the editor specified by the $EDITOR environment
variable with the protected password entry for that account. Simply find
and remove the "u_lock" entry, then save quit the editor.

For example:

This account is locked:

mcheek:u_name=mcheek:u_id#201:u_pwd=VIyfrxO1cdD.Y:u_succhg#865377576:\
        :u_unsucchg#865347935:u_policy:u_pwchanger=mcheek:u_oldcrypt#0:\
        :u_suclog#865205124:u_suctty=ttyp7:u_lock:chkent:

After removing the "u_lock" parameter on the third line, now this
account is unlocked:

mcheek:u_name=mcheek:u_id#201:u_pwd=VIyfrxO1cdD.Y:u_succhg#865377576:\
        :u_unsucchg#865347935:u_policy:u_pwchanger=mcheek:u_oldcrypt#0:\
        :u_suclog#865205124:u_suctty=ttyp7:chkent:


Hope this helps.
Matt
